response.body:
@bradfitz updated, PTAL. I deviated from what we discussed slightly because it gets irritating to test for writability when bruteforcing our way through possible paths.

Instead, I isolated the one special case, which is "system daemon on unix". For those, the CACHE_DIRECTORY envvar specifies where to dump files (this envvar is set if you use `CacheDirectory=...` in your systemd config).

All other cases, on all OSes, use `os.UserCacheDir`, which resolves to a good place.

